description: Security standards for arbitrage trading system
---
# Security Standards

## Critical Security Rules

### 1. Secret Management

**NEVER commit secrets:**
```rust
// BAD - Will be caught by pre-commit hooks
const API_KEY: &str = "sk_live_abc123xyz";
let api_key = "sk_live_abc123xyz";

// GOOD - Load from environment
let api_key = std::env::var("EXCHANGE_API_KEY")
    .expect("EXCHANGE_API_KEY must be set");
```

**Secret Storage:**
- Use environment variables for all API keys
- Use `.env.example` with placeholder values (never real keys)
- Use a secrets manager (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault) for production
- Rotate keys regularly (every 90 days minimum)

**Pre-commit Hook:**
```bash
# Check for secrets before commit
gitleaks detect --source=. --verbose
```

### 2. Input Validation

**Validate ALL external input:**

```rust
// Order size validation
fn validate_order_size(size: Decimal, min: Decimal, max: Decimal) -> Result<()> {
    if size < min {
        return Err(ArbitrageError::Validation("Order below minimum".into()));
    }
    if size > max {
        return Err(ArbitrageError::Validation("Order above maximum".into()));
    }
    if size % tick_size != Decimal::ZERO {
        return Err(ArbitrageError::Validation("Invalid lot size".into()));
    }
    Ok(())
}

// Price validation
fn validate_price(price: Decimal) -> Result<()> {
    if price <= Decimal::ZERO {
        return Err(ArbitrageError::Validation("Price must be positive".into()));
    }
    if price > MAX_REASONABLE_PRICE {
        return Err(ArbitrageError::Validation("Price exceeds maximum".into()));
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

### 3. Network Security

**Rate Limiting:**
```rust
// Implement per-IP and per-API-key rate limits
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct RateLimiter {
    per_ip: DashMap<String, TokenBucket>,
    per_key: DashMap<String, TokenBucket>,
}
```

**TLS Requirements:**
- Use TLS 1.2+ for all external connections
- Validate certificates (never disable verification)
- Use pinned certificates for critical exchanges

**DoS Protection:**
- Implement request timeouts (5 second default)
- Reject requests exceeding size limits
- Use circuit breakers for external API calls

### 4. Order Execution Safety

**Kill Switch Pattern:**
```rust
pub struct KillSwitch {
    enabled: AtomicBool,
    max_order_value: AtomicDecimal,
    allowed_exchanges: AtomicUset<ExchangeId>,
}

impl KillSwitch {
    pub fn can_execute(&self, exchange: ExchangeId, value: Decimal) -> bool {
        if !self.enabled.load(Ordering::SeqCst) {
            return false;
        }
        if value > self.max_order_value.load(Ordering::SeqCst) {
            return false;
        }
        self.allowed_exchanges.load().contains(&exchange)
    }
}
```

**Max Slippage Validation:**
```rust
fn validate_slippage(expected_price: Decimal, actual_price: Decimal) -> Result<()> {
    let slippage = ((actual_price - expected_price) / expected_price).abs();
    if slippage > MAX_ALLOWED_SLIPPAGE {
        return Err(ArbitrageError::SlippageExceeded {
            expected: expected_price,
            actual: actual_price,
            threshold: MAX_ALLOWED_SLIPPAGE,
        });
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

### 5. Data Integrity

**Order Book Integrity:**
```rust
fn validate_order_book(book: &OrderBook) -> Result<()> {
    // Check bids < asks (no arbitrage within single exchange)
    let best_bid = book.bids.first().map(|b| b.price);
    let best_ask = book.asks.first().map(|a| a.price);
    
    if let (Some(bid), Some(ask)) = (best_bid, best_ask) {
        if bid >= ask {
            return Err(ArbitrageError::InvalidOrderBook(
                "Best bid >= best ask".into()
            ));
        }
    }
    
    // Check prices are positive
    ensure_positive_prices(book)?;
    
    // Check amounts are positive
    ensure_positive_amounts(book)?;
    
    Ok(())
}
```

### 6. Error Handling

**Never expose internals in errors:**
```rust
// BAD - Leaks internal details
#[error("Database error: {0}")]
DatabaseError(String),

// GOOD - Generic error, no internal details
#[error("Service temporarily unavailable")]
ServiceUnavailable,
```

**Log securely:**
```rust
// Never log sensitive data
log::info!("Order placed for {} on {}", symbol, exchange); // OK
log::debug!("API response: {:?}", response); // BAD if contains keys

// Use structured logging without sensitive fields
log::info!(
    "Order executed: id={}, symbol={}, side={}",
    order.id, order.symbol, order.side
);
```

### 7. Concurrency Safety

**Thread-Safe Types:**
```rust
// Use appropriate concurrency primitives
use tokio::sync::{Mutex, RwLock, Semaphore};
use std::sync::Arc;

// For single-reader, multi-writer: RwLock
// For single-state, multi-access: Mutex
// For rate limiting: Semaphore
// For hot paths with many readers: DashMap
```

**Panic Safety:**
```rust
// Use panic guards for critical sections
let _guard = panic::panic_hooks::set(|| {
    // Emergency stop on panic
    kill_switch.trigger("panic in trading thread");
});
```

### 8. Audit Trail

**Log ALL trading decisions:**
```rust
#[derive(Debug, Serialize)]
pub struct TradeDecision {
    timestamp: chrono::DateTime<Utc>,
    opportunity_id: Uuid,
    exchanges: (ExchangeId, ExchangeId),
    expected_profit: Decimal,
    actual_profit: Option<Decimal>,
    status: DecisionStatus,
}

impl TradeDecision {
    pub fn log(&self) {
        // Persist to immutable audit log
        audit_log.push(self.clone());
    }
}
```

### 9. Dependency Security

**Regular Audits:**
```bash
# Check for vulnerabilities
cargo audit

# Check for outdated dependencies
cargo outdated

# License compliance
cargo deny check licenses
```

### 10. Security Checklist

Before deploying to production:
- [ ] All API keys loaded from environment/secrets manager
- [ ] Rate limiting configured
- [ ] Kill switch implemented and tested
- [ ] Max slippage validation enabled
- [ ] TLS verification enabled
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in code
- [ ] Input validation on all external data
- [ ] Error messages don't leak internals
- [ ] Audit logging enabled
- [ ] Dependencies audited (cargo audit)
- [ ] Panic handlers defined for critical threads
